{"duration_api_ms":116481,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0204548c-a824-57b7-bea3-1783011bc81a","total_cost_usd":0.6877322,"usage":{"input_tokens":18,"cache_creation_input_tokens":40240,"cache_read_input_tokens":503220,"output_tokens":13246,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2083},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":40240,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1318,"cache_read_input_tokens":72264,"cache_creation_input_tokens":346,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":346},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1607,"outputTokens":31,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0001762,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":18,"outputTokens":13246,"cacheReadInputTokens":503220,"cacheCreationInputTokens":40240,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.687556,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":2083,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":40240,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01UmnnCncGPqUCNPKEHNF8DU","tool_input":{"command":"sed -n '/^## 4/,/^## 5/p;/^## 6/,$p' .theseus/spec/method-measurement.md | head -150; cat .theseus/METHOD-CHANGELOG.md | head -30; ls .theseus/proposals; cat .theseus/scoreboard/packets.jsonl .theseus/scoreboard/friction.jsonl"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_018EfBf4TJnGXc3dYBXazUMa","tool_input":{"command":"python3 -I - <<'E'\nimport json,collections as C\nR=[json.loads(l) for l in open('.theseus/scoreboard/packets.jsonl')]\nids=set(r['id'] for r in R);print(len(R),len(ids))\nfor k in ['result','type','executor']:print(k,C.Counter(r.get(k) for r in R))\ng=C.defaultdict(list)\nfor r in R:\n  if r['result']=='discarded':continue\n  g[(r['executor'],r['type'])].append(r)\nfor k,v in sorted(g.items()):\n  d=[x for x in v if x['result']=='done']\n  print(k,len(v),'done',len(d),'cost',round(sum(x['cost_usd'] for x in v),2),'1st',sum(1 for x in d if x.get('approved_first_review')),'att',sum(x['attempts'] for x in v))\nprint('total cost',round(sum(r.get('cost_usd',0) for r in R),2),'rev',round(sum(r.get('reviewer_cost_usd',0) for r in R),2),'min',round(sum(r.get('duration_min',0) for r in R),1))\nd=[r for r in R if r['result']=='done'];print('done',len(d),'first',sum(r.get('approved_first_review',False) for r in d))\nbl=[r for r in R if r['result']=='blocked'];print('blocked cost',round(sum(r['cost_usd'] for r in bl),2),[r['id'] for r in bl])\nE\nls .theseus/scoreboard/runs/PKT-0009"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_014sRmbC85PFVEg9mKM8x7Je","tool_input":{"command":"cd .theseus/proposals && cat > TEP-0001.md <<'E'\n---\nid: TEP-0001\ntitle: Record the tool version and the section 4.1 fields on every scoreboard record\norigin: AUD-1\ncomponent: factory\ntarget: method-measurement#4.1, method-measurement#3\nstatus: proposed\n---\n\n## Problem\nAll 28 records of AUD-1 lack `estimated`, `context_ratio`, `out_of_context_reads`, `spawned_packets`, `rejection_reasons`, `block_reason`, `flaky_oracle`, so 4 of 7 indicators of §4.4 cannot be computed. All records say `method_version: 0.1.0` while friction F8, F12, F13, F16, F19 cite tool fixes in Theseus 0.7.1–0.9.0, so no fix can be measured before/after.\n\n## Proposed change\nIn §4.1 add: \"The factory writes every field of this section on every record; a missing value is written as `null`, never omitted. Each record also carries `tool_version` (the Theseus CLI version that ran the packet).\" In §3 add: \"A change to the tooling that alters packet flow bumps the method patch version.\"\n\n## Hypothesis\nAfter the change, at least 95% of new records contain all §4.1 keys and `tool_version`, and AUD-2 can compute at least 6 of the 7 §4.4 indicators, with no increase in median factory overhead per packet above 5%.\n\n## How to verify\nCount keys in records written after the version bump (minimum 20 records). Count computable indicators in AUD-2.\n\n## Risks\nAgents may fill `out_of_context_reads`/`context_ratio` with guesses; check variance and spot-check against run folders.\nE\ncat > TEP-0002.md <<'E'\n---\nid: TEP-0002\ntitle: Attribute every block to method, model or task\norigin: AUD-1\ncomponent: routing\ntarget: method-measurement#4.1 block_reason\nstatus: proposed\n---\n\n## Problem\nAll 7 blocked records of AUD-1 (PKT-0002 x2, PKT-0004, PKT-0011, PKT-0013, PKT-0009 x2) were caused by tooling or rules (friction F5, F6, F8, F12, F13, F16), yet they count against the executor model. 5 of them are Sonnet records and make Sonnet/characterize look 1/6 at first review. Blocked attempts cost $13.92 (40% of spend).\n\n## Proposed change\n`block_reason` becomes `{\"cause\": \"method\" | \"model\" | \"task\", \"ref\": \"<rule or spec section>\", \"text\": \"...\"}`, set by the integrator/reviewer when a packet is blocked. Routing statistics (§4.4 Routing) exclude records with `cause: method`, and the audit reports method-caused block cost as its own indicator.\n\n## Hypothesis\nWith attribution, method-caused blocked cost falls below 15% of total spend within the next 20 packets (because it becomes visible and alarmable), and routing approval rates per model change by no more than the noise once method blocks are excluded.\n\n## How to verify\nAUD-2: share of blocked records with a `cause`; method-caused block cost / total cost; first-review rate per model with and without method blocks (minimum 20 packets).\n\n## Risks\nAttribution bias toward \"method\" to protect a model's numbers; the auditor samples run folders to check.\nE\ncat > TEP-0003.md <<'E'\n---\nid: TEP-0003\ntitle: One friction schema, enforced by theseus validate\norigin: AUD-1\ncomponent: factory\ntarget: method-measurement#4.3\nstatus: proposed\n---\n\n## Problem\nFriction lines F1–F11 follow §4.3 (`role`, `model`, `hindered/missing/unneeded` with `ref`); F12–F21 use `phase`, `kind`, `note` without `ref`, `role` or `model`. Half the period's friction cannot be counted per rule.\n\n## Proposed change\n§4.3: \"Every friction line has `packet`, `role`, `model`, `date` and at least one of `hindered`, `missing`, `unneeded`, `helped`, each an object with `ref` and `text`. `theseus validate` rejects other shapes.\"\n\n## Hypothesis\n100% of friction lines written after the change pass validation, and at least 80% carry a `ref` that resolves to a spec or adapter section, without reducing friction lines per finished packet (currently 21 / 21 packets).\n\n## How to verify\nRun `theseus validate` on friction.jsonl; count lines per packet in AUD-2 (minimum 20 packets).\n\n## Risks\nStricter format may discourage reporting; watch lines per packet.\nE\ncat > TEP-0004.md <<'E'\n---\nid: TEP-0004\ntitle: Reviewer checks the executor log and the Spawned packets section\norigin: AUD-1\ncomponent: review\ntarget: prompts/reviewer.md\nstatus: proposed\n---\n\n## Problem\nPKT-0010 and PKT-0012 were approved with an empty executor log (F15); PKT-0009 was approved without the follow-up it was told to spawn (F18, F19); PKT-0002 was approved after a surprising behaviour was dropped from the tests (F7).\n\n## Proposed change\nAdd to the reviewer prompt: \"Reject if the Executor log is empty, if the packet asked for follow-ups and Spawned packets (or `.theseus/spawn/`) does not list them, or, for characterize packets, if a surprising behaviour mentioned in the log is not kept in a test.\"\n\n## Hypothesis\nIn the next 20 done packets, 0 are approved with an empty executor log and 0 requested follow-ups are missing at approval, with first-review approval staying at or above 60% (currently 70%).\n\n## How to verify\nScan done packets in AUD-2 for empty logs and compare requested vs spawned follow-ups; first-review rate from packets.jsonl.\n\n## Risks\nMore rejections for paperwork; the balancing first-review rate shows it.\nE\ncd ../.. && test -s .theseus/audits/AUD-1.md && echo OK && git add .theseus/audits .theseus/proposals && git commit -qm \"docs(method): add AUD-1 audit and TEP-0001..0004 proposals\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GfMVS4GJ2FBm26wB5X9Aot\" && git log --oneline -1"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":16,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I wrote the first method audit, AUD-1, and four change proposals, TEP-0001 to TEP-0004, and committed them (`7066a6e`). The acceptance check `test -s .theseus/audits/AUD-1.md` passes.\n\n**Two limits on this audit:**\n- **Same model family:** I audited as claude-opus-5-5, the same family as every executor and reviewer in the period. The spec prefers a different family, so a second audit by a GPT model would be worth running.\n- **Shell refusals:** my Python script for the numbers and some `sed`/heredoc commands were refused. I didn't work around that: I counted the indicators by hand from `packets.jsonl`. I also didn't go through `.theseus/scoreboard/runs/` attempt by attempt.\n\n**What the scoreboard shows:** 28 records cover 21 packets. 20 records ended done, 7 blocked and 1 discarded (PKT-0019).\n- **First-review approval:** 14 of 20 done records (70%).\n- **Spend:** $34.59 in total. Reviews cost $6.53 of that (19%).\n- **Blocked attempts:** they cost $13.92 (40% of spend), and PKT-0009 alone cost $11.26.\n- **Escapes:** none, but the whole period is one day, so zero means nobody has looked yet, not that there are none.\n\n**Main findings:**\n1. **Most indicators can't be measured yet.** No record has the per-packet fields the spec requires (estimated size, context ratio, out-of-context reads, spawned packets, block reason, and others). Four of the seven indicators can't be computed.\n2. **The version never changed.** Every record says `method_version 0.1.0`, although the friction log mentions tool fixes in Theseus 0.7.1 through 0.9.0. So no fix can be compared before and after.\n3. **All 7 blocks came from the method or tooling, not the model.** They are still charged to the executor. Five are Sonnet records, which makes Sonnet look poor on `characterize` packets (1 of 6 approved at first review).\n4. **The friction log has two formats.** Lines 12–21 lack the rule reference, role and model that the spec asks for, so they can't be counted per rule.\n5. **Reviewers don't check the executor log or requested follow-ups.** Two packets were approved with an empty log, and PKT-0009 was approved without the follow-up it was asked to create.\n\nFollowing the spec's sample-size rule, anything affecting fewer than 20 packets is labelled an observation. Only findings 1 and 2 are firm, because they touch every record.\n\n**Decisions:**\n- **Two proposals first:** TEP-0001 (record the tool version and all required fields) and TEP-0002 (tag each block as caused by the method, the model or the task). The spec allows at most two changes per version, and without these two no later proposal can be verified.\n- **Not proposed:** the merge conflicts on ignore files (project adapter only) and the unclear diagnosis scoring direction (a wording fix). Neither is a method change.\n- **No follow-up packets requested.**\n\n**Keep as is:** the independent second diagnosis (it caught a real defect in PKT-0007), cross review, resuming a blocked packet from its branch, spawn requests, and small migrate packets (4 of 4 approved at first review).\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas:**\n- Record which tool version each packet ran under, or later audits can't tell which fixes helped.\n- Mark blocks caused by the method separately from blocks caused by the model.\n\nBoth are recorded in AUD-1. I didn't write them into the packet's Atlas section.\n\nFiles are in `.theseus/`:\n- `audits/AUD-1.md`\n- `proposals/TEP-0001.md`\n- `proposals/TEP-0002.md`\n- `proposals/TEP-0003.md`\n- `proposals/TEP-0004.md`","ttft_ms":1659,"type":"result","duration_ms":116621,"uuid":"35409012-ae0d-453c-ab76-985036086c52","ttft_stream_ms":910,"time_to_request_ms":387,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":6,"system_prompt":224,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":19,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":7,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":7,"init_frame_send":6,"engine_pickup":7,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":11,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":35,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":37,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":1,"request_build":8},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":118,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":297,"time_to_request_major_faults":4,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":216,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":141,"process_rss_mib_result":230,"process_anon_mib_result":140,"process_peak_rss_mib":235,"process_cpu_ms_turn":2991,"process_wall_ms_turn":116620,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":1963,"process_wall_ms_streaming":110864,"main_stream_count":9,"main_stream_event_count":1900,"main_stream_chunk_count":1671,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_ope